{"name":"Mincemeat","hex":"#b66a3c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mincemeat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of fruit, spices and suet used as a filling for mince pies.","Minced meat, mince."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mincemeat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mincemeat","blocks":[{"text":"Mincemeat is a mixture of chopped apples and dried fruit, distilled spirits or vinegar, spices, and optionally, meat and beef suet. Mincemeat is usually used as a pie or pastry filling. Traditional mincemeat recipes contain meat, notably beef or venison, as this was a way of preserving meat prior to modern preservation methods. Modern recipes often replace the suet with vegetable shortening or other oils and/or omit the meat. However, many people continue to prepare and serve the traditional meat-based mincemeat for holidays."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Making_Mince_pies_-_tarts_in_baking_tray.jpg/330px-Making_Mince_pies_-_tarts_in_baking_tray.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mincemeat","wikidata":"Q1553789"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Mincemeat_from_Flickr_user_Stuart_Caie.jpg/500px-Mincemeat_from_Flickr_user_Stuart_Caie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Mincemeat_from_Flickr_user_Stuart_Caie.jpg/1280px-Mincemeat_from_Flickr_user_Stuart_Caie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Mincemeat_from_Flickr_user_Stuart_Caie.jpg/500px-Mincemeat_from_Flickr_user_Stuart_Caie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mincemeat","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMincemeat_from_Flickr_user_Stuart_Caie.jpg"},{"s